@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

Sixty-eight requirements in eleven groups, every one at status draft until the G1 requirements gate baselines the set. Each group names the need it traces to and the scoping decision of 2026-10-06 that fixed it. The Steelbore Standard §20.6 sentence pattern applies throughout: a binding obligation is carried by shall, a prohibition by shall not.

Priority is mandatory, expected or optional; only the first two count toward the §17 progress figures. Verification is one of the four §21.1 methods --- test, analysis, inspection, review of design --- chosen when the requirement was written. Milestone names the plan item that discharges the requirement; Assurance appears only where a requirement belongs to a raised Category A subsystem (the password agent and the initrd lifecycle unit).

