@node Progress Requirements
@section Progress

Source: FRN-NEED-002; decision 3 (hybrid progress). A time estimate in the initrd, where no D-Bus exists, and the real systemd Manager.Progress after switch-root, mapped onto one bar.

@anchor{FRN-SRS-010}
@subheading FRN-SRS-010 --- Initrd bar from the cached initrd duration
@cindex FRN-SRS-010
@table @asis
@item Requirement
In the initrd, the bar shall display 0.30 times the elapsed time divided by the cached initrd duration, clamped to the range 0.00 to 0.30.
@item Rationale
No D-Bus exists before switch-root; the cache is the best available signal. Scaled rather than clamped, so the initrd's share of the bar fills over the whole initrd instead of stalling at 30 % of it; the wording was amended in draft to the formula the design and the code use, for confirmation at G1. The cache is read from /sysroot/var/lib/fairing once the root is mounted; until then the first-boot curve applies.
@item Source
@ref{FRN-NEED-002}, decision 3.
@item Priority
mandatory
@item Verification
test
@item Status
draft
@item Milestone
M2
@end table

@anchor{FRN-SRS-011}
@subheading FRN-SRS-011 --- First-boot curve reaches 0.30 at 8 s
@cindex FRN-SRS-011
@table @asis
@item Requirement
